{"author":{"id":"8d7a7fea5b07a0d5d081edd516d55afeb51ce9c18b2b2be6ceb30eb17cd9b547"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794426458,"nonce":"JQXCoebg/HLga6EIOyJwXuBZjAE=","title":"No Wayland window position or session restore: xdg-session-management-v1 missing in winit 0.30","message":"Found while probing how much window and view state a program can read and set from outside (Blinc fs-blinc-3, winit 0.30.13, wgpu 26, KWin 6.8.2 run as `kwin_wayland --virtual`, one and two outputs).\n\nPosition\n- `WindowConfig.position` goes to `with_position`, `center` to `set_outer_position` (extensions/blinc_platform_desktop/src/window.rs). Under Wayland both have no effect: winit's Wayland `set_outer_position` is empty (\"Not possible on Wayland\") and `with_position` is not evaluated.\n- Repro: start any windowed app with a position (e.g. 300,200, or 1500,100 with a second output) or with `center`. The window stays at 140,36 in the virtual KWin.\n- Reading is not possible either: winit's Wayland `outer_position()` returns `Err(NotSupported)`, and Blinc does not expose the winit window after start.\n- The protocol itself (`xdg_toplevel`) has no position; this holds for every compositor.\n\nSession restore\n- KWin 6.8.2 advertises `xdg_session_manager_v1` v1 (checked with `wayland-info`). The protocol (xdg-session-management, staging; bindings are in `wayland-protocols` 0.32.13) lets the compositor remember position, size, output and maximized per toplevel (`add_toplevel` / `restore_toplevel`, session token as a string). It is the standard way to restore window placement on Wayland.\n- winit 0.30 does not speak it and does not hand out the `xdg_toplevel`. Other compositors were not checked.\n\nConsequence for FreeSynergy\n- Do not save a window position. Do not use KWin rules or a KWin script over D-Bus as a workaround (both work on KDE only and either touch user configuration or flash at the old place).\n\nFollow-up work\n- A. Read window state: a handle in `WindowedContext` with inner size, maximized, fullscreen, outer position (Option), monitor name, plus a change callback. Small. Without it \"maximized\" cannot be read, so a saved size would store the screen size.\n- B. Choose the output at start: `WindowConfig.monitor`, via `available_monitors()`, `Borderless(Some(m))` for fullscreen. Later.\n- C. `xdg-session-management` once winit can hand out the toplevel (winit patch or raw `wl_display` client). Larger; later.\n- D. app_id under Wayland: a name field in `WindowConfig`, `WindowAttributesExtWayland::with_name` in `apply_platform_attrs` (only the X11 `with_name` is used today). Small.\n\nA and D are small and are carried in the fork (fs-blinc-4). B and C later.","files":null}]}